COMMERCIAL S11 DATABASE MIGRATION PRIVILEGE DIAGNOSIS

Status: ROOT_CAUSE_CONFIRMED; AUTOMATIC_ROLLBACK_GREEN
Observed SQLSTATE: 42501 INSUFFICIENT_PRIVILEGE

The r4 deployment passed source preflight, exact private backup verification,
canonical release synchronization and repository switching. It then failed
before migration 0031 committed. The versioned controller automatically
restored both source repositories, package, units and configuration. S7, S8,
S10 and nginx returned active with zero restarts; S11 tables and files are
absent and both repositories are clean at their source commits.

A transaction-only diagnostic executed the exact frozen migration and always
rolled it back. PostgreSQL returned permission denied for schema public. The
configured runtime DSN is intentionally least-privilege and cannot create
tables. The SQL and required predecessor schema objects were otherwise present.

Bounded correction:
- Use the already established local `runuser -u postgres -- psql` migration
  ingress for the exact hash-verified migration file, streamed over stdin.
- Use the same local administrator only for the controller's versioned feature
  flag update.
- Keep all runtime service access and evidence reads on the existing
  least-privilege DSN.
- Do not broaden runtime grants and do not add credentials.

Backup and rollback:
- The r4 predeploy backup is complete, exact-mode private and immutable.
- The automatic non-destructive rollback completed successfully.
- The retry requires a fresh timestamped backup and exact r5 freeze.
- Immutable freezes r1 through r4 are not moved.

Validation contract:
- Focused and full Control tests, shell syntax, JSON and secret scan pass.
- PR CI, same-SHA review, merge-commit and post-merge CI pass.
- The exact annotated r5 freeze binds the canonical Application and Control
  commits and trees before any retry.
